.TH "CSSMATHVALUE" "3JS" "August 11, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
CSSMathValue \- CSSMathValue
.SH SYNOPSIS
\f[B]Note:\f[R] This feature is available in Web Workers.
.PP
The \f[B]\f[CB]CSSMathValue\f[B]\f[R] interface of the CSS Typed Object
Model API is the base interface for objects representing complex numeric
values produced by the CSS \f[CR]calc()\f[R], \f[CR]min()\f[R],
\f[CR]max()\f[R], and \f[CR]clamp()\f[R] functions.
.RS
.PP
\f[B]Note:\f[R] \f[CR]CSSMathValue\f[R] cannot be constructed directly.
Instances are returned by the platform (for example via
\f[CR]StylePropertyMapReadOnly.get()\f[R]) as one of its subtypes,
listed below.
.RE
.SH INSTANCE PROPERTIES
.TP
\f[B]CSSMathValue.operator\f[R] \f[I](read\-only)\f[R]
Returns the operator that the current subtype represents.
.SH STATIC METHODS
\f[I]Also inherits methods from its parent interface,
\f[CI]CSSNumericValue\f[I].\f[R]
.SH INSTANCE METHODS
\f[I]Also inherits methods from its parent interface,
\f[CI]CSSNumericValue\f[I].\f[R]
.SH INTERFACES BASED ON CSSMATHVALUE
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]CSSMathClamp\f[R]
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]CSSMathInvert\f[R]
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]CSSMathMax\f[R]
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]CSSMathMin\f[R]
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]CSSMathNegate\f[R]
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]CSSMathProduct\f[R]
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]CSSMathSum\f[R]
.SH EXAMPLES
.SS \f[CR]calc()\f[R] representations
This example shows how the \f[CR]operator\f[R] property identifies the
operation represented by a \f[CR]calc()\f[R] value\(cqs
\f[CR]CSSMathValue\f[R] subtype, including for a nested value.
.SS HTML
.IP
.EX
<\f[B]div\f[R] id=\(dqdemoBox\(dq>Text</\f[B]div\f[R]>
.EE
.SS CSS
\f[CR]width\f[R] is set using a \f[CR]calc()\f[R] subtraction, which is
represented as a \f[CR]CSSMathSum\f[R] whose second term is negated.
.IP
.EX
demoBox {
  \f[B]width\f[R]: calc(30% \- 20px);
}
.EE
.SS JavaScript
We read the \f[CR]width\f[R] value using \f[CR]computedStyleMap()\f[R],
then log its \f[CR]operator\f[R] and the \f[CR]operator\f[R] of its
nested value.
.IP
.EX
\f[B]const\f[R] styleMap = document.querySelector(\(dq#demoBox\(dq).computedStyleMap();
\f[B]const\f[R] width = styleMap.get(\(dqwidth\(dq);

log(\(gatype: ${width.constructor.name}\(ga);
log(\(gaoperator: ${width.operator}\(ga);
log(\(ganested value type: ${width.values[1].constructor.name}\(ga);
log(\(ganested value operator: ${width.values[1].operator}\(ga);
.EE
.SS Result
\f[CR]width\f[R] is represented by a \f[CR]CSSMathSum\f[R] object whose
\f[CR]operator\f[R] is \f[CR]\(dqsum\(dq\f[R], because
\f[CR]calc(30% \- 20px)\f[R] is represented as an addition of
\f[CR]30%\f[R] and the negation of \f[CR]20px\f[R].
The second nested value\(cqs type is \f[CR]CSSMathNegate\f[R] and its
\f[CR]operator\f[R] is \f[CR]\(dqnegate\(dq\f[R] (reflecting that
negation).
